  "gaps": [
    "Residency rules are stated only as credit counts, not tied to specific courses: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) must be completed at UMGC, half the credits within the major must be completed at UMGC, and at least 15 upper-level (300–499) credits must be completed at UMGC; the capture does not say which ledger items must satisfy these.",
    "At least half the major credits must be earned through graded coursework (not exam, certification, portfolio, or noncollegiate training); which specific major courses must be graded is not stated.",
    "The capture does not list which upper-level CCJS courses may substitute for CCJS 350, CCJS 360, or CCJS 352 beyond 'any upper-level CCJS course'.",
    "Specific courses that satisfy the Mathematics block are listed only as options (MATH 105, MATH 107, MATH 115, MATH 140, STAT 200, or department-approved); the recommended sequence suggests MATH 105, but no single course is mandated.",
    "The 1-credit Research and Computing Literacy item's '(1 credit)' label is split across columns in the capture; the credit value is taken from that block, and the block total of 7 is consistent with it.",
    "Credits earned by examination limits: only that no more than 3 writing credits may be earned by examination; other examination or prior-learning limits for this major are not stated in the capture.",
    "Minimum grade of C applies to major courses and a 2.0 overall GPA is required; these are policy conditions, not ledger items."
  ],
